## Suggested Data Model

A starting relational design could include:

| Table | Example fields | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `customers` | `customer_id`, `name`, `phone`, `email`, `created_at` | Core customer profile |
| `consents` | `consent_id`, `customer_id`, `channel`, `status`, `timestamp`, `source` | Record communication permissions and withdrawals |
| `services` | `service_id`, `service_name`, `category`, `price` | Service catalog |
| `visits` | `visit_id`, `customer_id`, `visit_date`, `total_amount` | Salon visit history |
| `visit_services` | `visit_id`, `service_id`, `amount` | Services delivered during each visit |
| `loyalty_transactions` | `transaction_id`, `customer_id`, `type`, `points`, `visit_id`, `created_at` | Auditable points earning and redemption ledger |
| `campaigns` | `campaign_id`, `name`, `channel`, `audience`, `status` | Campaign configuration |
| `campaign_events` | `event_id`, `campaign_id`, `customer_id`, `event_type`, `timestamp` | Delivery and engagement events |

These are **proposed tables**, not a deployed database schema. Fields, constraints, retention periods, and access policies will be finalized during implementation.

## Lifecycle Marketing Strategy

| Stage | Example trigger | Example communication | Primary KPI |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Welcome | New customer enrolls | Membership welcome and benefits | Enrollment completion |
| Post-visit | Completed salon visit | Thank-you and service follow-up | Repeat-visit rate |
| Engagement | Customer reaches a loyalty milestone | Points or reward update | Reward redemption rate |
| Retention | Customer has not visited within an expected interval | Relevant return-visit offer | Returning customers |
| Win-back | Extended period of inactivity | Personalized reactivation campaign | Reactivation rate |

Campaign triggers, timing, eligibility, and frequency caps should be tested and adjusted based on actual salon behavior. Promotional messages must honor the customer's channel preferences and applicable rules.

## Email Template Library

The repository will hold reusable, mobile-friendly HTML mailers for:

- Welcome and loyalty enrollment
- Post-visit thank-you messages
- Loyalty balance and reward eligibility
- Seasonal and promotional offers
- Inactive customer reactivation

Templates should use email-compatible HTML/CSS, meaningful alternative text, accessible contrast, clear calls to action, and tested personalization placeholders. Preview and test in common email clients before production use.

