## Implementation Roadmap

- [ ] **Phase 1 — Discovery:** Confirm customer enrollment process, staff roles, reward rules, and success metrics.
- [ ] **Phase 2 — Data foundation:** Design schema, build registration, implement duplicate checks and consent capture.
- [ ] **Phase 3 — CRM operations:** Record visits and services; provide customer lookup and profile management.
- [ ] **Phase 4 — Loyalty MVP:** Configure earning and redemption rules; maintain transaction history.
- [ ] **Phase 5 — Communications:** Create and test HTML templates; integrate a messaging provider and opt-out handling.
- [ ] **Phase 6 — Automation:** Launch welcome, post-visit, and reactivation journeys with safeguards.
- [ ] **Phase 7 — Analytics and launch:** Validate dashboards, test end-to-end flows, train staff, and monitor results.

## Success Metrics

| Metric | Definition |
| --- | --- |
| Enrollment rate | New loyalty enrollments ÷ eligible customers invited |
| Repeat-visit rate | Customers with 2+ visits in a defined period ÷ customers visiting in that period |
| Customer retention | Customers returning in a defined follow-up window ÷ eligible cohort |
| Reward redemption rate | Redeemed rewards ÷ issued eligible rewards |
| Campaign click-through rate | Unique clickers ÷ delivered emails, where trackable |
| Reactivation rate | Inactive customers who return after a campaign ÷ targeted inactive customers |

All metrics require explicit date windows, eligibility criteria, and event definitions before reporting.

## Privacy, Security & Responsible Messaging

- Collect only information necessary for customer service and the loyalty program.
- Provide a clear privacy notice and capture channel-specific marketing permissions as appropriate.
- Support opt-outs, consent changes, correction, and deletion requests where applicable.
- Restrict staff access by role; secure data in transit and at rest.
- Avoid uploading real customer data, credentials, provider API keys, or private campaign exports to GitHub.
- Use synthetic customer records for development and demos.
- Review applicable Indian data protection and electronic messaging requirements before launch.

